    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Shifted exponents are often designed so the bracket is small.\n\n2^(n−1)+2^(n+1)=320.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Factor 2^(n−1):\n\n2^(n−1)(1+4)=320\n2^(n−1)=64=2^6\nSo n−1=6 and n=7.\n\nNotice the final +1 step; 6 is the exponent n−1, not n.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
